{"type":"text","text":"# Sheet 3 — SMB World 1-1 HUD RAM map\n\nAll three found with **no reference** (the session is blind-calibrated, so `lookup_symbol` returned nothing) and recorded with `source: \"differential search\"`; `promote_mappings` succeeded (mapping file now has 13 addresses).\n\n## The addresses\n\n| Value | Addresses | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Coin count** | `$07ED` (tens), `$07EE` (ones) | 2 bytes, **one decimal digit per byte**, BCD |\n| **Level timer (TIME)** | `$07F8` (hundreds), `$07F9` (tens), `$07FA` (ones) | 3 bytes, one decimal digit per byte; counts 400 → 000 |\n| **Score** | `$07DD`–`$07E2` | 6 bytes, one decimal digit per byte, **most significant first** (millions … tens); the displayed ones place is a fixed `0` tile, so the screen shows these digits followed by 0 |\n\n## How I got there\n\nStart on the title began a real game (score 000000, coins x00, TIME 394) after the attract demo confused the first attempt — during the demo the HUD shows the demo's accumulated score and input is ignored.\n\n**Coins.** Snapshot → jump into the first ? block from below (`+1 coin, +200 pts`) → snapshot → `diff increased` = **127 survivors**; second ?-block coin → `diff increased` `from` the first = **17 survivors**, in which `$07EE` went **1 → 2** (the ones digit) and `$07E1` went **2 → 4** (the score's hundreds digit, 200→400).\n\nRaw last-round hits included: `0x07EE old 1 new 2`, `0x07E1 old 2 new 4`, `0x03F0`, `0x0748`, `0x075E`, `0x030F`, `0x0317` (all 1→2 / 2→4 coincidences in sprite/OAM and copy buffers).\n\n**Timer.** An idle interval diffed `decreased` left 19 survivors incl. `$07F9`; reading `$07F8-$07FA` gave `3,3,0` while the screen read **TIME 330**, and `2,6,6` while it read **266**.\n\n**Proof (write + screenshot).**\n- *Timer:* wrote `$07FA=9` (screen 266) → after one tick RAM read 8 and the HUD showed **TIME 268**. Full extent: wrote `$07F7=1, $07F8=3, $07F9=0, $07FA=0, $07FB=2` → after one tick RAM was `1,2,9,9,2` and the screenshot showed **TIME 299** — the neighbours `$07F7`/`$07FB` never appeared.\n- *Coins & score:* the HUD is event-driven (a raw RAM write does **not** appear immediately), so I wrote a distinctive pattern (`$07DC..$07E4 = 9,1,2,3,4,0,5,6,7`; `$07ED=3, $07EE=5`) and forced a full status-bar redraw by setting the timer to `001` and letting the time-up death reload the level. The screenshot showed **MARIO 1234050** and **x35** — exactly the six bytes `$07DD..$07E2` in order plus the fixed ones-place `0`, and the coin pair `3,5`. The bytes written one past each end (`$07DC`, `$07E3`, `$07E4`) never showed; `$07DC` was even cleared to 0 by the reload.\n\nTwo HUD quirks worth knowing: the digits are **not** redrawn every frame (only when the game itself changes the value), and the score has no RAM ones digit — the trailing `0` is a fixed tile."}
